# Chart the Brain Review Surface

## Finish line

The Brain wiki gains a write path: rendered pages become review surfaces whose annotations return to agents as structured input. Accepted by Joel 2026-07-24; testable as written:

1. Any rendered page at brain.joelclaw.com accepts inline annotations from any tailnet device, phone included.
2. Submitting writes a `.svx` receipt committed to the annotated note's owning repo, carrying page, commit-at-review-time, author surface, and spans; the next graph rebuild shows it as a node backlinked to the page.
3. The gateway correlates the annotation on a flowId and delivers it to the owning session or loop; a joelclaw agent acts on it with no explanation needed.
4. One real HITL step in an active brief blocks, notifies Joel with its page URL, and closes through this loop end to end.
5. Maintenance: HITL steps use the loop by default once live, so daily use is the regression test; a brainbench/wikibench leg asserts the receipt round-trip stays healthy, so breakage is loud, not discovered mid-review.

## Vocabulary

- **annotation** — inline feedback on a rendered Brain page, anchored to text spans, pinned to the commit the page rendered at review time.
- **receipt** — the committed `.svx` record of an annotation; a graph node with provenance, backlinked to the annotated page.
- **write path** — the chain from browser submit to committed receipt (the wiki is a static build today; this is the live part this effort adds).
- **return path** — gateway delivery of an annotation to the owning session or loop, correlated on a flowId.
- **interception** — a blocked `interaction: HITL` step that notifies with its page URL and closes through the annotation loop.
- **stopgap** — the clipboard feedback-boxes loop on the bugle map; ships as-is, retired by the receipt path at parity.

## Notes

- **Domain**: extends the live Brain page renderer (brain.joelclaw.com/&lt;root&gt;/&lt;slug&gt;, provenance per page) with annotation write-back. Adjacent maps, do not duplicate: [Chart the joelclaw Brain Graph](../brain-graph/brain-graph-brief.svx) owns the graph projection and renderer; [joelclaw Bugle redesign](../bugle-redesign/bugle-redesign-brief.svx) owns the toolbar and the feedback-boxes stopgap; privacy is owned by [Define Privacy, Access, and Publication Boundaries](../personal-wiki/define-privacy-access-publication-boundaries.svx) — any team reopen goes through it, never re-decided here.
- **Single-operator scope** (Joel, 2026-07-24): team is out of this finish line; it stays latent and charters as its own effort once this loop is touchable.
- **Interception is in the finish line** (Joel, 2026-07-24): without a blocking case the loop has no forcing function.
- **Feedback boxes ship as the stopgap** (Joel, 2026-07-24, "let it ship"): the bugle ticket stays claimed and ships clipboard-only; this map retires it at parity, same pattern as the static-page stopgap.
- **Plannotator is prior art only** (Joel, 2026-07-24): cited for its ideas (annotation returning to agents, decision-time interception); no dependency, no install anywhere in the fleet.
- **Phone-first UX** (Joel, 2026-07-24): if annotation is not comfortable on the phone over the tailnet, condition 1 fails — the point is reviewing where flagg's terminal isn't.
- **Inherited fixed direction**: SvelteKit + MDSvX, Effect v4, tailnet-only stands, receipts are `.svx` by Brain law; build work lands in `joelhooks/joelclaw-wiki`; this brief lives here for adjacency with its siblings.
- **Skills every session should consult**: `/skill:grill-master`, `/skill:brain-first-workflow`, `/skill:effect`, `/skill:tailnet-topology`, `/skill:messaging` (gateway contract), `/skill:joel-writing-style` when available.

## Decision ledger

<!-- one line per closed step: gist + link -->

- [Research How Annotation Systems Anchor Spans to Mutable Documents](./research-annotation-anchoring.svx) — Pin quote and position selectors to the reviewed commit's rendered-text projection, re-anchor through diff plus context, and preserve uncertain matches as visible unanchored receipts.

## Latent

- Team: shared-repo brain roots give team read almost structurally; identity, per-root visibility, and per-author receipts force reopening the privacy boundaries ticket — deliberately, by a new fact.
- Annotations as an observational-memory input stream: receipts are the highest-signal observations the write-loop map could distill.
- Toolbar integration: an annotate mode beside secureMode in the JoelClaw toolbar (bugle map's build-joelclaw-toolbar).
- Annotating editions (the immutable layer) versus Brain pages (mutable, commit-pinned) — the anchor model may differ.

## Out of scope

- Installing plannotator anywhere in the fleet — prior art only (Notes).
- Team auth, tiers, and identity — past this finish line; returns as a fresh effort through the privacy ticket.
- Replacing the feedback-boxes stopgap before the receipt path reaches parity — it ships on the bugle map untouched.
